<problem><title>Video review questions</title>

<setup>
<function name="h" variables="x">x/2+1/(18) x^3</function>
<math name="equilibria" unordered="true">-3,3,0</math>
</setup> 


<p>Given the discrete dynamical system
  <me>x _{n+1} = h(x_n) \;\; \text{where} \;\; h(x) = $h</me>
whose function evolution rule, <m>h(x)</m> is graphed below,
</p>  

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title>Determine equilibria</title> 
<p>What are the 3 equilibria?
  <answer name="vid1Review1" matchPartial="true" unorderedCompare="true">
    <award>$equilibria</award>
  </answer>
  (<ref to="doenet:7FRM6VWrzPKk1bwC2SKx72">Remind me how to find equilibria...</ref>)
</p>
<p><em>Enter equilibrium values separated by commas</em></p>
</exercise>
  
<module copy="doenet:83jD1JShkD8umrK9bSc1v8" xmin="-4" xmax="7" ymin="-4" ymax="7" function="$h" initialInitialValue="1" initialValueDx="0.25" checkInitialCondition="false" x0="3" showNavigation="false" cobwebbingWeight="0" attractThreshold="0.2" grid="true" name="cobweb_cubic" />  

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title>Determine stability using cobwebbing</title>
<p>Cobweb using the applet above starting at <m>x_0 = 2.5</m>. Do the values for <m>x_n</m> tend towards or away from the equilbrium at <m>E = </m> <answer name="equilibriumAns">3</answer> ? <em>(type the closest equilbrium value)</em>
  <answer>
    <choice>Towards the equilibrium</choice>
    <choice credit="1">Away from the equilibrium</choice>
  </answer>
  (<ref to="doenet:7GavdebJoto83FLcbNqFQV">Remind me how to cobweb...</ref>)
</p>
  
 <hint><title>Starting picture</title>
  <p>For starters, your cobwebbing should look something like this:</p>
<module copy="doenet:83vCskTYActBRJRjUApuoe" xmin="-4" xmax="7" ymin="-4" ymax="7" function="$h" x0="2.5" showNavigation="false" numPoints="4" attractThreshold="0.2" grid="true" name="cobweb_sol1" />
  </hint>

<p>Cobweb using the applet above starting at <m>x_0 = 3.5</m>. Do the values for <m>x_n</m> tend towards or away from the equilbrium at <m>E = $equilibriumAns</m> 
  <answer>
    <choice>Towards the equilibrium</choice>
    <choice credit="1">Away from the equilibrium</choice>
  </answer>
</p>

  <hint><title>Starting picture</title>
  <p>For starters, your cobwebbing should look something like this:</p>
<module copy="doenet:83vCskTYActBRJRjUApuoe" xmin="-4" xmax="7" ymin="-4" ymax="7" function="$h" x0="3.5" showNavigation="false" numPoints="4" attractThreshold="0.2" grid="true" name="cobweb_sol2" />
  </hint>

<p>Is the equilibrium at <m>E = $equilibriumAns</m> stable or unstable?
  <answer>
    <choice>stable</choice>
    <choice credit="1">unstable</choice>
  </answer>
</p>
</exercise>


<solution>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title>Determine equilibria</title>
  Equilibria are -3,0,3.
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title>Determine stability using cobwebbing</title>
  <ol>
    <li>For <m>x_0 = 2.5</m> the values tend away from the equilibrium.</li>
    <li>For <m>x_0 = 3.5</m> the values tend away from the equilibrium.</li>
    <li>For <m>E = 3</m> the equilibrium is unstable.</li>
  </ol>
</exercise>  
</solution>
  
</problem>
